    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Founded in 1852 as a frontier post, Lancaster is one of Dallas County's earliest settlements.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lancaster%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1890 the Lancaster Tap Railroad linked the town to the Houston & Texas Central main line at Hutchins, knitting Lancaster into regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dfwblogger.com/2025/10/21/the-history-of-lancaster-texas/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s historic square, damaged by an F4 tornado in 1994, remains a centerpiece of Lancaster’s downtown charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dfwblogger.com/2025/10/21/the-history-of-lancaster-texas/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Across from the historic square, the Lancaster Area Chamber and Visitors Center sits in the old Interurban Building that electrified the area in 1911.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tourtexas.com/destinations/57",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The White and Company Bank building, a local landmark since 1898, was rebuilt after a tornado and now houses the Lancaster Economic Development Corporation.",
